    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "VictoriaMetrics"
      },
      "description": "APPROXIMATION. This compares two independently computed percentiles; the difference of two percentiles is NOT the percentile of the difference. Treat it as an indicator of coordination and network overhead, never as an exact decomposition of a request. The line is the coordinator percentile minus the worst local table percentile on the same node. It indicates how much of the client's wait is spent outside the local read path: replica selection, inter-node messaging, and waiting for the slowest replica in the quorum. A negative value is not an error; it means the two percentiles came from different request populations, which is exactly why this is an approximation.",
      "fieldConfig": {
        "defaults": {
          "color": {
            "mode": "palette-classic"
