    {
      "datasource": {
        "type": "prometheus",
        "uid": "VictoriaMetrics"
      },
      "description": "The fraction of bloom filter checks that said 'maybe present' for a key the SSTable did not hold. On a healthy workload this sits at or near zero. A rising ratio means SSTables are being opened and read needlessly, which shows up as extra SSTables per read and higher local read latency. The usual causes are a bloom_filter_fp_chance that is too loose for the table, or a filter that no longer fits in memory. Note this is a lifetime ratio reported by the node, not a windowed rate.",
      "fieldConfig": {
